course: dictionary
lesson: 9895
title: The word taker
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A taker is a person who takes or accepts something that is offered. The ending -er often means a person who does something, so a taker is someone who takes. «Any takers?» means "Does anyone want this?"
explain: Compound words show the same pattern. A risk-taker is someone who takes risks, and a test-taker is someone who sits a test. In «The most important thing to tell the call taker is where you are», the words around call taker tell you the job: the call taker answers calls and needs to know where you are.
explain: A taker can also mean someone who takes more than they give. «Leaders were not always takers» means some leaders grabbed more than they shared. In stories about fairness, a taker is the opposite of a giver.
fact: A taker is a person who takes or accepts something that is offered.
fact: A taker can be someone who takes more than they give.
fact: In compound words, -taker means a person who does something: risk-taker, note-taker, test-taker.
fact: «Any takers?» means "Does anyone want this?"
fact: «No takers» means nobody wants it.
exercise: «Any takers?» the teacher asked, holding up the last biscuit. What does she mean? | Is it time to go home? | *Does anyone want this? | Who has taken my pencil?
exercise: In «The most important thing to tell the call taker is where you are», what is a call taker? | A phone that is broken | A person who sings loudly at school | *A person who answers emergency calls
exercise: What is a risk-taker? | Someone who counts the coins in a jar | *Someone who does things that might be dangerous | Someone who always plays safe
test: «Leaders were not always takers.» What does taker mean here? | A person who runs very fast | Someone who gives away everything they own | A person who paints pictures | *Someone who takes more than they give
test: Which word means a person who takes notes in class? | painter | *note-taker | teller | giver
exam: Which phrase means that nobody wants the offer? | test-taker | any takers | giver and taker | *no takers
